    "note": "Read Amended 2019-04-25 (text of the only floor vote). The change strikes 'or in the state prison' from subdivision (c): the possession offense is no longer punishable by state prison. Subdivisions (a), (b), (d) reprinted unchanged."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 29805 (Penal Code): (c) Any person who is convicted, on or after January 1, 2020, of a misdemeanor violation of Section 25400, 25850, or 26350, and who, within 10 years of the conviction, owns, purchases, receives, or has in possession or under custody or control, any firearm, is guilty of a public offense, punishable by imprisonment in a county jail not exceeding one year, by a fine not exceeding one thousand dollars ($1,000), or by both that imprisonment and fine."
